<div class="helparticlelist margin-bottom--25-25-25">
 

 



    

    

    
	    

    <section class="article-list">

        <h2 class="article-list--heading">Create campaigns, ad groups, keywords, and more with the Apple Ads Platform API</h2>
        <p class="article-list--desc">The Apple Ads Platform API is designed to let developers, agencies, and third-party platforms manage campaigns and pull reports programmatically. It includes client libraries in multiple languages to help you integrate quickly. Use them to programmatically manage campaigns, ad groups, and keywords on the App Store, along with ads on Apple Maps.</p>

		

    </section>

 

    
    
</div>
<div class="helparticlelist margin-bottom--25-25-25">
 

 



    

    

    
	    

    <section class="article-list">

        
        <p class="article-list--desc"><a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/apple-ads-platform-api" class="article-copy-block-link icon icon-after icon-external" aria-label="Access the API documentation and see complete details">Access the API documentation and see complete details</a>
<br class="br-l br-m br-s no-space" /><br class="br-l br-m br-s no-space" />
To implement the Apple Ads Platform API effectively, you’ll need to understand the technical requirements and plan ahead to ensure you have the resources needed to develop and maintain the application.
</p>

		

    </section>

 

    
    
</div>
<div class="helparticlelist margin-bottom--25-25-25">
 

 



    

    

    
	    

    <section class="article-list">

        <h2 class="article-list--heading">Access the Apple Ads Platform API </h2>
        <p class="article-list--desc">Apple Ads uses OAuth 2 to authenticate API requests. To access the Apple Ads Platform API within your own organization, you’ll need to create or designate an API user: 
</p>

		

        <ol role="list" class="">
             <li role="listitem">
	Have an Account Admin sign in to your Apple Ads account. 
   
</li>
        
             <li role="listitem">
	Go to the User Management tab within Account Settings. 
   
</li>
        
             <li role="listitem">
	Edit or invite a new user and assign them one of the following roles: API Account Manager, API Account Read Only, Limited Access API Read &amp; Write, or API Read Only.   
</li>
        
             <li role="listitem">
	After your API user is set up, have them sign in to your Apple Ads account and go to the API tab within Account Settings. 
   
</li>
        
             <li role="listitem">
	On the API page, they can create a client by following the steps outlined in the <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/apple_ads/implementing-oauth-for-the-apple-search-ads-api">API documentation</a>. For additional details on making calls against the API, refer to the documentation.     
</li>
        </ol>

                   

		

    </section>

 

    
    
</div>
<section class="article-copy-block margin-bottom--25-25-25">










































    
        
        
  
        
        







    
        

        

 		
		
		


        


		


		

		


        

        

        
		
					
                    
        






   

    
        
        
  
        
        







    
        

        

 		
		
		


        


		


		

		


        

        

        
		
					
                    
        






   

    
        
        
  
        
        







    
        

        

 		
		
		


        


		


		

		


        

        

        
		
					
                    <p class="article-copy-block--description ">Note that if a user’s role changes from an API user to a non-API user, their API access will be revoked. In addition, API access for users associated with the deleted user will also be revoked.</p>
        






   

    
        
        
  
        
        






    
    
    
    
    
    
    
        
        
    
        
      
    






   

    

































</section>
<div class="helparticlelist margin-bottom--25-25-25">
 

 



    

    

    
	    

    <section class="article-list">

        <h2 class="article-list--heading">Grant Apple Ads Platform API access to a third-party service provider</h2>
        <p class="article-list--desc">If you work with a campaign management partner or mobile measurement provider, your Apple Ads Account Admin or Campaign Group Manager can grant them access to your Apple Ads account through the use of a secure Apple sign in. Each Account Admin or Campaign Group Manager can grant access to only one third-party service provider per Apple Ads account at a time. <br class="br-l br-m br-s no-space" /><br class="br-l br-m br-s no-space" /> 
Here’s how to get started: </p>

		

        <ol role="list" class="">
             <li role="listitem">
	If your service provider has secure Apple sign in set up, go to the Authorizations section within their platform and click the Sign in with Apple button.   
</li>
        
             <li role="listitem">
	Sign in to Apple Ads as an Apple Ads Account Admin or Campaign Group Manager.   
</li>
        
             <li role="listitem">
	Choose the Apple Ads account that you’d like the service provider to be able to access.   
</li>
        
             <li role="listitem">
	Select the type of access you’d like to provide. Note that Read and Write and Read Only roles will be shared across any new campaign groups created for accounts that have ads on both Maps and the App Store.
<ul><li>Read and Write: Read reports and manage campaigns for all campaign groups.</li><li>Read Only: Read reports and view campaigns for all campaign groups.</li><li>Limited Access: Read reports and either manage or view campaigns only for specific campaign groups.</li></ul>   
</li>
        </ol>

                   

		

    </section>

 

    
    
</div>
<section class="article-copy-block margin-bottom--25-25-25">










































    
        
        
  
        
        







    
        

        

 		
		
		


        


		


		

		


        

        

        
		
					
                    
        






   

    
        
        
  
        
        







    
        

        

 		
		
		


        


		


		

		


        

        

        
		
					<h2 class="article-copy-block--heading ">Review or revoke Apple Ads Platform API service <br class="no-br-l no-br-m no-br-s no-space" />provider access</h2>
                    
        






   

    
        
        
  
        
        







    
        

        

 		
		
		


        


		


		

		


        

        

        
		
					
                    <p class="article-copy-block--description ">To review third-party API access, go to the API tab within Account Settings. Third-party approvals may be revoked at any time by selecting from the list of authorized service providers and choosing Revoke Access from the Actions menu.
</p>
        






   

    
        
        
  
        
        








 	
    

	


	


        

         

        



		

        

        

     
     

    

    

    







   

    
        
        
  
        
        






    
    
    
    
    
    
    
        
        
    
        
      
    






   

    

































